A glob view prints a JSON file's first three scalar keys as a field summary, with `...` when more follow; a file with only objects and arrays, or a root array, has nothing to summarize, and a leading comment is the header.
== args
input
== file input/package.json
{
  "name": "demo",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": {},
  "license": "MIT"
}
== file input/small.json
{"a": 1, "b": [2]}
== file input/objects.json
{"a": {}, "b": []}
== file input/list.json
[1, 2]
== file input/commented.json
/* Editor settings. */
{"a": 1}
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/commented.json: Editor settings.
input/list.json: (no header available)
input/objects.json: (no header available)
input/package.json: {name: "demo", version: "0.1.0", private: true, ...}
input/small.json: {a: 1}
== stderr
== exit 0
